From fd406aa243c02b492492753992e16ccdaa161bec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alan Tsai <alan-tsai@quantatw.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 10:48:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] i2c-vr: add support for MPS MP2940x VR firmware update

The MP2940x image configuration rows before the END marker are parsed
and written through Page 3 command 0x2B for the first 128 rows and
Page 3 command 0x2A for the remaining rows.

The update flow follows the vendor timing requirement: wait 40 ms after
the first row of each 128-row unit and 3 ms after the remaining rows.
The current update flow supports only non-PEC transfers.

Related PR:
entity manager
https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/entity-manager/+/93710
https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/entity-manager/+/93714

phosphor dbus interfaces
https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/+/93186

The corresponding change is under review in Gerrit [1].
[1] https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-bmc-code-mgmt/+/93437

Tested on rainiera6.
'''
